{
  "frozen_descriptor": "A tall, thin humanoid figure, roughly 1.9 meters in height, clad in a floor-length hooded black robe typical of a medieval plague doctor. Its head is covered by a pale ceramic beak mask that appears permanently fused to the flesh beneath it, the eye openings dark and smooth. The mask shows no seams or joins, and the robe conceals most of the body, leaving only the hands exposed. Those hands are bare, with ordinary skin tones, and the fingers are long and dexterous. The entity carries no visible equipment or tools. The organic integration of mask to head is seamless, with no gaps or visible attachment points.",
  "entity_sheet": "SCP-049 is the plague-doctor entity — the single most recognizable trait is its fused ceramic avian mask. It leaves behind reanimated corpses (SCP-049-2 instances) as its signature aftermath, a grotesque parody of its claimed cure. Its presence is often preceded by a faint smell of old leather and chemical preservatives.",
  "story_logline": "A gentle, deluded doctor who sincerely believes he cures a hidden plague — yet his touch brings instant death and his \"cure\" turns the dead into shambling things. The video uncovers the hollow tragedy behind the mask.",
